        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3eda21e7-2ff6-5368-8a91-10526494648a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danie Visser, Oliver Marach, Rick Leach, Jim Pugh, Grant Connell, Glenn Michibata, Pieter Aldrich\n- Events: 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles\n- Organizations: ATP Masters Series\n- Concepts: Grand Slam men's doubles, doubles rankings\n\nFacts:\n- The ATP Masters Series was one of the most prestigious sets of men's professional tennis tournaments after the four Grand Slam events.\n- Danie Visser was a doubles specialist who won three Grand Slam men's doubles titles, including two Australian Open titles and one US Open title.\n- At the 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles, defending champions Rick Leach and Jim Pugh lost in the semifinals to Grant Connell and Glenn Michibata.\n- At the 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles, Pieter Aldrich and Danie Visser won the title by defeating Grant Connell and Glenn Michibata 6–4, 4–6, 6–1, 6–4 in the final.\n- Oliver Marach reached a career-high doubles ranking of world No. 8 on October 18, 2010.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "83385ef5-b625-5110-afe0-c68b2ba27ecb",
        "text": "Page: Danie Visser. Sentence: A doubles specialist, he won 3 Grand Slam men's doubles titles (2 Australian Open and 1 US Open).\nPage: Oliver Marach. Sentence: His career high in doubles is world No. 8, set on October 18, 2010.\nPage: 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles. Sentence: Rick Leach and Jim Pugh were the defending champions, but lost in the semifinals to Grant Connell and Glenn Michibata.\nPage: 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles. Sentence: Pieter Aldrich and Danie Visser won the title, defeating Connell and Michibata 6–4, 4–6, 6–1, 6–4, in the final.\nPage: ATP Masters Series. Sentence: The tournaments were important for the top male players on the professional circuit as the series constituted the most prestigious tournaments in men's tennis after the four Grand Slam events.",
